# Acceleration Unit Tests
# NOTE: Slash-caret notation (m/s^2) and "per" multi-word forms (meters per second squared)
# are not yet parseable as unit targets due to lexer/parser limitations.
# Use named aliases: standard-gravity.
# The conversion registry supports m/s^2, ft/s^2, cm/s^2 internally.

## Basic acceleration values
a1 = 9.80665 standard-gravity
# Expected: 9.80665 standard-gravity

## Acceleration arithmetic
total = 5 standard-gravity + 5 standard-gravity
# Expected: 10 standard-gravity
